// tests/fixtures/err_arena_escapes_nested_mismatch.ubl
// GAP 2 — Escape Boundary Enforcement (docs/MEMORY_MODEL.md §6 / §3).
//
// Both `outer_list` and the reassigned value are "MID tier" and both
// come from a `with arena(...)` block — but they are TWO DIFFERENT,
// non-interchangeable arenas (ArenaId(1) vs ArenaId(2), per §3).
// `outer_list` is declared under the outer arena; reassigning it from
// inside the nested arena hands it a value that dies when the INNER
// block ends, while `outer_list` itself lives until the OUTER block
// ends. This is exactly the scenario MEMORY_MODEL.md §3 calls out by
// name, and is why arena-membership checks must always compare the
// *specific* ArenaId, never just "is/isn't tagged ArenaRef."
//
// Expected: sema FAIL (ArenaRefEscapesBoundary).

@tier(mid)
fn nested() void {
    with arena(64KB) {
        let mut outer_list = List.new()
        with arena(64KB) {
            outer_list = List.new()
        }
    }
}

fn main() void {
    nested()
}
